{
	"comments": [
		{
			"id": 1940895,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone/post/3lz6udnp3dc2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lynn",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/lynn.zone",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/98763b5ab4dd50bd2062b54313357e4b9d9c0537de0daa590f4126f8e966fbd8.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T12:26:11.000Z",
			"content": "`scrollbar-gutter` is great, but I don&apos;t know if I&apos;d go so far as to argue that everyone should be putting it in their resets. As far as I&apos;m aware, there&apos;s currently no way to put *anything* in the space it reserves, which unfortunately makes it awkward to use with some pretty common layouts",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1940896,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us/post/3lz6zkbc42s2m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bramus",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/e2611e6594c5759b0d7cf84058fbf5875b3fdc62a0494095224e8baff59d3921.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T13:59:22.000Z",
			"content": "As long as you don’t go for `scrollbar-gutter: stable both-edges`, you should be fine.\n\nReason: Chrome has a bug in which the gutter is doubled up on “retina” devices: <a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40064879\">issues.chromium.org/issues/40064...</a>\n\n(The bug is assigned, and I heard engineering will look at it next quarter)",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1940897,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us/post/3lz6znkz6u22m",
			"author": {
				"name": "Bramus",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.bsky.app/e2611e6594c5759b0d7cf84058fbf5875b3fdc62a0494095224e8baff59d3921.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-19T14:01:13.000Z",
			"content": "There’s still some discussion on how viewports should behave in this case.<br>\n<br>\nWhat the WG did resolve on – but this hasn’t been implemented anywhere (????) – is that top layer content (such as a modal dialog and its backdrop, or a fullscreen video) can draw on top of the reserved space.",
			"type": "reply",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1941451,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://jeffbridgforth.com/weeknotes-september-21-2025/",
			"author": {},
			"date": "2025-09-21T23:10:33.000Z",
			"content": "",
			"type": "mention",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1942275,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/did:plc:lyk2pixxcmyeu4jrapaq26fy/post/3lzqqgs7k322n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Piccalilli",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/piccalil.li",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/conocybe.us-west.host.bsky.network/29b8dd7bcc3f775209cac5cba73211e324c77855390d4f9174d076de8ed52b50.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-26T15:04:14.000Z",
			"content": "A great usage of the new(ish) scrollbar-gutter property. \n\n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/stable-scrollbar-gutters/\">www.zachleat.com/web/stable-s...</a>",
			"type": "mention",
			"via": "webmention"
		},
		{
			"id": 1946797,
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mas.to/@CSSence/115362380986438275",
			"author": {
				"name": "Matthias Zöchling",
				"url": "https://mas.to/@CSSence",
				"avatarUrl": "https://avatars.webmention.io/cdn.masto.host/ead615ec62dd8daf9419df05f75686984c21ddd74876236d8782e7f02b43bd3b.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-10-12T17:30:37.000Z",
			"content": "<p>Tired:<br />`html { overflow-y: scroll; }`</p><p>Wired:<br />`html { scrollbar-gutter: stable; }`</p><p>Nice little <a href=\"https://mas.to/tags/CSS\">#<span>CSS</span></a> gem from <span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span>.<br /><a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/stable-scrollbar-gutters/\"><span>https://www.</span><span>zachleat.com/web/stable-scroll</span><span>bar-gutters/</span></a></p><p>The feature detection is the cherry on top.</p>\n<a class=\"p-category\" href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/tags/css\">css</a>\n<a class=\"u-mention\" href=\"https://mas.to/tags/CSS\"></a>\n<a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/stable-scrollbar-gutters/\">A tiny bit-o-CSS for Stable Scrollbar Gutters—zachleat.com</a>",
			"type": "mention",
			"via": "webmention"
		}
	],
